- ### Editing in place
+ ### Edición en el sitio

- A graph is sometimes built up one edge at a time, as when a build system discovers tasks or a
- scheduler accepts jobs. A `Topology` keeps its topological order valid as edges arrive. A new
- edge disturbs only the nodes between its two ends.
+ A veces un grafo se construye arista a arista, como cuando un sistema de compilación descubre
+ tareas o un planificador acepta jobs. Una `Topology` mantiene válido su orden topológico a medida
+ que llegan aristas. Una arista nueva solo altera los nodos situados entre sus dos extremos.

- A `Topology` is a mutable value with one exclusive owner. It is edited through its methods,
- which do not produce new values:
+ Una `Topology` es un valor mutable con un único dueño exclusivo. Se edita mediante sus métodos,
+ que no producen valores nuevos:

= which do not produce new values:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val topology = Topology[Text]()
+ val topology = Topology[Text]()

- topology.add(t"app", t"lib")
+ topology.add(t"app", t"lib")

- topology.add(t"lib", t"core")
+ topology.add(t"lib", t"core")

= topology.add(t"lib", t"core")
- ```
+ ```

= topology.add(t"lib", t"core")
= ```
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= topology.add(t"lib", t"core")
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= topology.add(t"lib", t"core")
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
- ##
+ ##

- Out.println(topology.linearized.inspect)
+ Out.println(topology.linearized.inspect)

= Out.println(topology.linearized.inspect)
- ```
+ ```

- An edge which would close a cycle is refused with a `Dag.Error`, and the graph is left as it
- was:
+ Una arista que cerraría un ciclo se rechaza con un `Dag.Error`, y el grafo queda como estaba:

= was:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

- typecheck
+ typecheck

= typecheck
- ##
+ ##

- topology.add(t"core", t"app")
+ topology.add(t"core", t"app")

= topology.add(t"core", t"app")
- ```
+ ```

- When the editing is done, the topology is given up. `Topology.freeze(topology)` and
- `Dag(topology)` both consume it, so the result can never be edited behind its back. A `Dag`
- thaws into a `Topology` with `thaw`, and `snapshot` takes a `Dag` without giving up the handle.
+ Cuando se termina de editar, se renuncia a la topología. `Topology.freeze(topology)` y
+ `Dag(topology)` la consumen ambos, de modo que el resultado nunca puede editarse a sus espaldas.
+ Un `Dag` se descongela en una `Topology` con `thaw`, y `snapshot` toma un `Dag` sin renunciar al
+ descriptor.

- ### Partial orders
+ ### Órdenes parciales

- A `Hasse` diagram takes a set and an ordering relation, and computes the covering structure: for
- each element, the elements immediately above and below it, with every implied comparison
- dropped. These are the divisors of 12, ordered by divisibility:
+ Un diagrama de `Hasse` recibe un conjunto y una relación de orden, y calcula la estructura de
+ cobertura: para cada elemento, los elementos inmediatamente por encima y por debajo de él, con
+ todas las comparaciones implícitas eliminadas. Estos son los divisores de 12, ordenados por
+ divisibilidad:

= dropped. These are the divisors of 12, ordered by divisibility:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val divisors = Hasse(Set(1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 12))((a, b) => b % a == 0)
+ val divisors = Hasse(Set(1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 12))((a, b) => b % a == 0)

= val divisors = Hasse(Set(1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 12))((a, b) => b % a == 0)
- ```
+ ```

= val divisors = Hasse(Set(1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 12))((a, b) => b % a == 0)
= ```
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= val divisors = Hasse(Set(1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 12))((a, b) => b % a == 0)
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= val divisors = Hasse(Set(1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 12))((a, b) => b % a == 0)
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
- ##
+ ##

- Out.println(divisors.parents(2).inspect)
+ Out.println(divisors.parents(2).inspect)

- Out.println(divisors.children(6).inspect)
+ Out.println(divisors.children(6).inspect)

- Out.println(divisors.maxima.inspect)
+ Out.println(divisors.maxima.inspect)

= Out.println(divisors.maxima.inspect)
- ```
+ ```

- A `Hasse` diagram is itself a graph, in which each element points at the elements it covers. It
- linearizes from its bottom to its top, and `divisors.dag` is the same relation as a `Dag`.
+ Un diagrama de `Hasse` es a su vez un grafo, en el que cada elemento apunta a los elementos que
+ cubre. Se linealiza desde su base hasta su cima, y `divisors.dag` es la misma relación como un
+ `Dag`.

- ### Layering
+ ### Estratificación

- `layered` arranges a `Dag` for drawing. Each node is assigned to a layer, with dependencies
- above dependents. The nodes within each layer are ordered so that the lines which join adjacent
- layers cross as rarely as possible. This is the layered approach of Sugiyama, which Graphviz's
- `dot` uses.
+ `layered` organiza un `Dag` para dibujarlo. Cada nodo se asigna a una capa, con las dependencias
+ por encima de los dependientes. Los nodos de cada capa se ordenan de modo que las líneas que unen
+ capas adyacentes se crucen lo menos posible. Es el método por capas de Sugiyama, que usa `dot` de
+ Graphviz.

= `dot` uses.
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val layering = dag.layered
+ val layering = dag.layered

= val layering = dag.layered
- ```
+ ```

- A node with no dependencies is in the first layer. Node `8` is two layers below, one for each
- dependency on its longest path. No link in this graph crosses another:
+ Un nodo sin dependencias está en la primera capa. El nodo `8` está dos capas más abajo, una por
+ cada dependencia de su camino más largo. Ningún enlace de este grafo cruza otro:

= dependency on its longest path. No link in this graph crosses another:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= dependency on its longest path. No link in this graph crosses another:
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= dependency on its longest path. No link in this graph crosses another:
=
